# System Analysis & Operational Report
**Project: BookStore C2C Marketplace**

## 1. Executive Summary
This extensive report details the architecture, operational flows, and advanced capabilities of the BookStore platform. The system is designed as a hybrid E-commerce platform that supports both **B2C** (Business-to-Consumer: Admin sells books) and **C2C** (Consumer-to-Consumer: Users sell used books).

The core differentiator is the **Secure Payment & Escrow System**, ensuring trust between buyers and sellers by holding funds until order confirmation.

---

## 2. System Architecture
The application follows a modern **MERN Stack** architecture (MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js), structured for scalability and maintainability.

### Tech Stack
-   **Frontend**: ReactJS (Vite), React Router v6, Context API (Auth, Cart), CSS Modules.
-   **Backend**: Node.js, Express.js.
-   **Database**: MongoDB (Mongoose ODM).
-   **Security**: JWT Authentication, HttpOnly Cookies, Password Hashing (Bcrypt), Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).

---

## 3. Database Schema (Class Diagram)
The following diagram illustrates the data models and their relationships.

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class User {
        +ObjectId _id
        +String name
        +String email
        +String password
        +Number walletBalance
        +String role (admin/user)
        +Boolean isBlocked
    }

    class Book {
        +ObjectId _id
        +String title
        +Number stock
        +Number price
        +ObjectId owner (User Ref - if C2C)
        +String condition
    }

    class Order {
        +ObjectId _id
        +ObjectId user (Buyer)
        +Enum escrowStatus (Held, Released, Refunded, Disputed)
        +OrderItem[] orderItems
        +Boolean isPaid
    }

    class Transaction {
        +ObjectId _id
        +ObjectId user (Owner of money)
        +String type (deposit, withdrawal, purchase, sale_income, refund)
        +Number amount
        +ObjectId relatedEntity (Order/User Ref)
    }

    User "1" -- "n" Book : Owns (Selling)
    User "1" -- "n" Order : Places
    User "1" -- "n" Transaction : Has
    Order "1" -- "n" Book : Contains
```

---

## 4. Operational Flows (Visualized)

### A. C2C Order & Escrow Flow (The Core Engine)
This flow ensures safety. Funds are deducted from Buyer but **HELD** by the system until the Buyer confirms receipt. Only then does the Seller get paid (minus 2% fee).

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Buyer
    participant System (Descrow)
    participant Seller
    participant Database

    Note over Buyer, System: Phase 1: Purchase
    Buyer->>System: Places Order (Payment: Wallet)
    System->>Database: VALIDATE: Buyer Balance >= Total?
    System->>Database: VALIDATE: Book Stock > 0?
    
    rect rgb(200, 255, 200)
        Note right of System: Atomic Transaction Start
        System->>Database: DEDUCT Buyer Wallet (-Amount)
        System->>Database: UPDATE Book Stock (-Qty)
        System->>Database: CREATE Order (Status: Held)
        System->>Database: LOG Transaction (Purchase)
    end
    
    System-->>Buyer: Order Success! (Funds Held)

    Note over System, Seller: Phase 2: Fulfillment
    Seller->>System: Checks "My Sales"
    System-->>Seller: Shows Order (Status: Packaging)
    Seller->>Buyer: Ships Item (Offline)

    Note over Buyer, System: Phase 3: Completion
    Buyer->>System: Confirms Receipt
    
    rect rgb(200, 200, 255)
        Note right of System: Fund Release
        System->>Database: UPDATE Order Status -> Completed
        System->>Database: UPDATE Escrow -> Released
        System->>Database: ADD Seller Wallet (+Amount - 2% Fee)
        System->>Database: LOG Transaction (Sale Income)
    end
    
    System-->>Seller: Notification: Funds Available!
```

### B. Dispute Resolution Flow
When things go wrong, the Admin acts as the judge via the Dispute Resolution Center.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Buyer
    participant Seller
    participant Admin
    participant System

    Buyer->>System: Request Refund (Reason: "Damaged")
    System->>System: Set Escrow -> "ReturnRequested"
    
    alt Seller Agrees
        Seller->>System: Confirm Refund
        System->>Buyer: Refund Money
        System->>Seller: Return Stock
    else Seller Rejects
        Seller->>System: Reject Refund (Reason: "Was perfect")
        System->>System: Set Escrow -> "Disputed"
        System->>Admin: Alert in Dispute Center
    end

    Note over Admin, System: Admin Intervention
    Admin->>System: Review Case
    
    alt Admin Sides with Buyer
        Admin->>System: EXECUTE "Refund"
        System->>Buyer: +Refund Amount
        System->>Book: +Restore Stock
    else Admin Sides with Seller
        Admin->>System: EXECUTE "Release"
        System->>Seller: +Income Amount
    end
```

---

## 5. Advanced Governance Capabilities

### Deep Analytics (The "See" Layer)
-   **Real-time Dashboard**:
    -   **User Growth**: Track platform adoption over the last 6 months.
    -   **Revenue Charts**: Daily income visualization.
    -   **Top Products**: Identifies best-selling books.
    -   **Inventory Alerts**: Auto-detects books with Stock < 10 for restocking.

### User 360 & Control
-   **Full Visibility**: Admin can view any user's complete Order History and Wallet Logs.
-   **Wallet Control**: Admin has the super-admin capability to manually **Adjust Balances** (Credit/Debit) for correcting errors or issuing bonuses.

---

## 6. Security & Safety Mechanisms
-   **Atomic Transactions**: Money never vanishes. If a database write fails during a transfer, the entire operation rolls back.
-   **Input Validation**: Strict checks on Stock and Wallet Balances (cannot go negative).
-   **Double-Entry Logging**: Every change in wallet balance corresponds to a `Transaction` record, ensuring full auditability.

